   "subject": "Re: Comparing growth curve models",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi,<div><br></div><div>Not sure if I understood it right, so feel free to correct me if I&#39;m wrong, but you seem to be interested in a cross-lagged panel model.</div><div>In this case, instead of creating a LGM to each variable, you should make a single model with both variables together and each variable at time t would be caused (regressed) by itself and the other variable at time t-1.</div><div><br></div><div>However, I understood you estimated a latent intercept and latent slopes of a non-linear function. In this case, I&#39;ve never seen anyone correlating intercepts and slopes of two different models. Maybe you could plot the line described by these functions and compare them.<br><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Yago</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
